  The app's text, in English, as the default resources — the fallback every
  device that matches no locale folder reads. Every key that is not marked
  translatable="false" is therefore required in every folder under
  values-<locale>/, and TranslationsTest holds them to that: a missing key is
  not a crash, it is a screen that silently drops back to English.

  A format specifier is part of the key's contract, not of the sentence: the
  positional arguments (%1$s, %2$d), the escaped literal percent (%%) and the
  XML escapes (\' for an apostrophe, \" around a quoted word) are identical in
  every translation, and the test compares them.
-->
